      "rationale": "The amber codon replaces the codon for A548, incorporating the UAA at position 548; the junction is therefore between N547 and A548 (insert_after_residue=547). Python confirmed residue 547=N and residue 548=A. The topology landmarks place residue 548 within the large extracellular domain (19\u2013567), 20 residues from TM1 (568), well clear of the TM boundary. The azi-CRD sensor is surface-labeled and reports agonist-driven conformational changes, confirming functional tolerance. Full-length mGluR2 expressed in HEK293T cells with an amber codon (TAG) at position A548 (azi-CRD); 4-azido-L-phenylalanine incorporated at this position in the cysteine-rich domain (CRD) was labeled with FRET dyes on the cell surface to generate a CRD conformational sensor.",
