      "rationale": "The amber codon is explicitly placed between E715 and V716 (insert_after_residue=715). Python confirmed residue 715=E and residue 716=V. The topology landmarks place this junction within the extracellular loop between TM4 (680\u2013700) and TM5 (726\u2013747), 15 residues from the TM4 boundary and 10 residues from TM5, well clear of both TM edges (\u22653 required). The azi-ECL2 sensor is surface-labeled and reports agonist-driven conformational changes, confirming functional tolerance. Full-length mGluR2 expressed in HEK293T cells with an amber codon (TAG) inserted between E715 and V716 (azi-ECL2); the unnatural amino acid 4-azido-L-phenylalanine was incorporated at this junction and labeled with FRET dyes on the cell surface to generate an inter-7TM domain conformational sensor.",
