      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "The signal peptide spans residues 1\u201318 (computed landmarks); the mature N-terminus begins at E19. A tag placed upstream of residue 19 would be cleaved with the signal peptide, so the correct junction is insert_after_residue=18 (residue_before=A, residue_after=E). Python confirmed residue 18=A and residue 19=E. The SNAP-tag construct is used across at least five independent publications for smFRET and surface-labeling experiments, all confirming plasma-membrane display and functional conformational sensing. Full-length mGluR2 expressed in HEK293T cells with SNAP-tag fused after the signal peptide (mature N-terminus, residue 19 onward); the VFT domain conformation was monitored by smFRET using donor/acceptor fluorophores conjugated to benzylguanine on the cell surface. Multiple independent studies (PMC9299836, PMC11972159, PMC10925283, PMC12394075, PMC11294631) use the identical construct architecture: signal peptide \u2192 HA epitope \u2192 SNAP-tag \u2192 mGluR2 cDNA, placing the tag extracellularly after signal-peptide cleavage at residue 18.",
